Translate k6 checks and thresholds into JMeter assertions and transaction-level error limits.

Translate the supplied k6 script to JMeter.

Execution contract: {"users": 2, "iterations": 2, "mode": "decline"}. Non-workload counts are iterations per user. One committed order per journey, no duplicate/extra carts. Two fixture variants count equally; the same artifact is reused without feedback. Fresh owner seeds are recorded after execution. Profiles: [{}, {"html_layout": 1, "reverse_catalog": true}]. Negative-control overrides: [{"decline_orders": true}].
Rubric/gates (per case: earned fraction capped by every prerequisite fraction; average all cases, never best case):
loads: 10 points — target loads Requires: none.
setup: 25 points — correct metric/transaction tagging Requires: loads.
behavior: 40 points — success and business-failure controls retain source outcomes Requires: loads, setup.
safety: 25 points — threshold scope and denominator exactly match the supplied contract. Requires: loads, behavior.
Malformed/non-executable artifacts earn zero execution-gated credit. A prerequisite fault can lose multiple checkpoints.

