Repair the supplied artifact.

Execution contract: {"users": 2, "iterations": 2, "mode": "threshold"}. Non-workload counts are iterations per user. One committed order per journey, no duplicate/extra carts. Two fixture variants count equally; the same artifact is reused without feedback. Fresh owner seeds are recorded after execution. Profiles: [{"checkout_delay_seconds": 0.01}, {"checkout_delay_seconds": 0.01, "html_layout": 1, "reverse_catalog": true, "catalog_delay_seconds": 0.5}]. Negative-control overrides: [{"checkout_delay_seconds": 0.5}].
Rubric/gates (per case: earned fraction capped by every prerequisite fraction; average all cases, never best case):
loads: 10 points — script loads Requires: none.
setup: 25 points — tags real checkout requests correctly Requires: loads.
behavior: 40 points — checkout-only metric/threshold responds to the injected slowdown Requires: loads, setup.
safety: 25 points — healthy control passes and slow control fails with the expected threshold evidence. Requires: loads, behavior.
Malformed/non-executable artifacts earn zero execution-gated credit. A prerequisite fault can lose multiple checkpoints.

Tag/name POST /v2/orders requests as "checkout" with a 250ms latency threshold/assertion.

